// Title: Execution of Powershell Script in Public Folder
// ID: fb9d3ff7-7348-46ab-af8c-b55f5fbf39b4
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Max Altgelt (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-04-06
// Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1059.001
// Description: This rule detects execution of PowerShell scripts located in the "C:\Users\Public" folder
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where ((process.executable endswith "\\powershell.exe" or process.executable endswith "\\pwsh.exe") and (process.command_line like "*_-f C:\\Users\\Public*" or process.command_line like "*_-f \"C:\\Users\\Public*" or process.command_line like "*_-f %Public%*" or process.command_line like "*_-fi C:\\Users\\Public*" or process.command_line like "*_-fi \"C:\\Users\\Public*" or process.command_line like "*_-fi %Public%*" or process.command_line like "*_-fil C:\\Users\\Public*" or process.command_line like "*_-fil \"C:\\Users\\Public*" or process.command_line like "*_-fil %Public%*" or process.command_line like "*_-file C:\\Users\\Public*" or process.command_line like "*_-file \"C:\\Users\\Public*" or process.command_line like "*_-file %Public%*"))
